>if soneone posts something on the Net regarding a nonprofit religious
>organization, what can you do ?


THIS IS NOT LEGAL ADVICE.  CONSULT A LAWYER BEFORE PROCEEDING.


Statements expressing an opinion (e.g. I think views of your religious
organization are the lowest form of stupidity), are completely
protected by the first amendment.  Consequently, they are not
actionable.

Statements expressing fact (e.g. the president of your religious
organization frequents prostitutes) may constitute defamation if they
are false.  In such cases you may be able to obtain a court order for
damages and/or a retraction.

The larger the group of people that the "fact" is about, the less
likely it is to be actionable.  (i.e. general statements about all
members of your religion, even if false, cannot be libelous, but
statements about a particular individual or small group of people, may
be).

