[...]

I know of no generally-accepted, comprehensive model of copyright for
copying *within* Netnews.

The main question such a model would have to answer is this: If a user
a site A posts some copyrighted-to-someone-else material to a
newsgroup and site B gets its feed from site A. Is site B libel for
copyright violation?

It should also tell us (in a noncircular way) which of the following
instances of copying within Netnews (if any) are permissible and why:
reposting, long excerpts, sites outside an article's "distribution"
copying that article, ftp archives, aliased newsgroups, filtered
newsgroups for high schools, etc.

(I don't have a comprehensive model, but I do have a partial model. I
